Chiming in with my 2 cents as I am working around this area. Correct me If I am wrong but I don't think it's ever going to be possible to go from a "string" key to a concrete key type in the context of reflection paths apart from primitive string/numeric types.

Or is the problem here, getting the "exact" primitive type?

If so could we not encode the `deserialization` info in the `Map` trait?

I.e.:
```rust
fn key_from_string(key: &str) -> Result/Option<Box<dyn PartialReflect>>
```

From a 3rd party crate POV I can get around this for a subset of types via:
```rust
fn map_key_to_concrete(key: &str, key_type_id: TypeId) -> Option<Box<dyn PartialReflect>> {
    let string_type_id = std::any::TypeId::of::<String>();
    let usize_type_id = std::any::TypeId::of::<usize>();

    match key_type_id {
        string_type_id => Some(Box::new(key.to_owned())),
        usize_type_id => key.parse::<usize>().ok().map(|u| Box::new(u) as Box<dyn PartialReflect>),
        _ => return None,
    }
}
```
etc..
